  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected pathway linking 7E-Tetradecen-1-ol to SNB-78 through multiple targets. The compound 7E-Tetradecen-1-ol is identified as a target of several molecules, including SNU-387, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, all of which are known to target SNB-78. This indicates that 7E-Tetradecen-1-ol may exert its biological effects through these intermediates, which in turn interact with SNB-78. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where 7E-Tetradecen-1-ol influences the activity of these compounds, which then modulate SNB-78. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 7E-Tetradecen-1-ol in the regulation of SNB-78 through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
